A solid ornament consists of a hemisphere on a closed cylinder. Both have radius $3$ cm, and the cylinder is $5$ cm high. Find the total surface area, including the bottom, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(-1.2,2)--(1.2,2)--(1.2,0)--cycle;
\draw (1.2,2) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(1.2,2);
\path (0.6,2) node[below] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (-1.2,1) node[left] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A solid model consists of a cone on a closed cylinder. Both have radius $2$ cm. The cylinder is $7$ cm high and the cone has slant height $6$ cm. Find the total surface area, including the bottom, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1,0)--(-1,2)--(1,2)--(1,0)--cycle;
\draw (-1,2)--(0,4)--(1,2);
\path (0,2)--(1,2) node[midway,below] {$2\text{ cm}$};
\path (-1,1) node[left] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,4)--(1,2) node[midway,right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

An ice-cream shape consists of a hemisphere joined to a cone. Both have radius $4$ cm, and the cone has slant height $7$ cm. Find the total outside surface area in exact form, in terms of $\pi$.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(0,-2.2)--(1.2,0)--cycle;
\draw (1.2,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\path (0,0)--(1.2,0) node[midway,above] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,-2.2)--(1.2,0) node[midway,right] {$7\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A capsule consists of a cylinder of diameter $6$ mm and length $11$ mm with a hemisphere attached to each end. Find its total surface area, rounded to the nearest whole square millimetre.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,-0.8)--(3,-0.8);
\draw (0,0.8)--(3,0.8);
\draw (0,0.8) arc[start angle=90,end angle=270,radius=0.8];
\draw (3,-0.8) arc[start angle=270,end angle=450,radius=0.8];
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.8)--(0,0.8);
\draw[dashed] (3,-0.8)--(3,0.8);
\path (1.5,-0.8) node[below] {$11\text{ mm}$};
\path (0,0) node[right] {$6\text{ mm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A square pyramid fits exactly on top of a square prism. The common square has side length $8$ m. The prism is $3$ m high, and each triangular face of the pyramid has slant height $5$ m. Find the total outside surface area, including the prism's bottom.

The exposed faces are one bottom square, four rectangular walls and four triangular faces. Representative faces:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (1.5,1.5);
\path (0.75,0) node[below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\draw (2.4,0) rectangle (3.9,0.7);
\path (3.15,0) node[below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (3.9,0.35) node[right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\draw (5,0)--(6.5,0)--(5.75,1.5)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (5.75,0)--(5.75,1.5);
\draw (5.75,0.18)--(5.93,0.18)--(5.93,0);
\path (5.75,0) node[below] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (5.75,0.9) node[right] {$5\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A cone sits on a closed cylinder of radius $6$ cm and height $4$ cm. The cone's perpendicular height is $8$ cm. Find the total surface area, including the bottom, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(-1.2,1.2)--(1.2,1.2)--(1.2,0)--cycle;
\draw (-1.2,1.2)--(0,3.2)--(1.2,1.2);
\draw[dashed] (0,1.2)--(0,3.2);
\draw (0,1.4)--(0.2,1.4)--(0.2,1.2);
\path (0,2.3) node[left] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.6,1.2) node[below] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (-1.2,0.6) node[left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A hemisphere is joined to a cone of the same radius, $5$ cm. The cone's perpendicular height is $12$ cm. Find the total outside surface area, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.1,0)--(0,-2.6)--(1.1,0)--cycle;
\draw (1.1,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.1];
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,-2.6);
\draw (0,-0.18)--(0.18,-0.18)--(0.18,0);
\path (0.55,0) node[above] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,-1.3) node[left] {$12\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A grain silo consists of a cylinder of radius $6$ m and height $8$ m with a hemisphere on top. Only its curved outside is painted; the bottom is not painted. Find the area to be painted, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(-1.2,2)--(1.2,2)--(1.2,0)--cycle;
\draw (1.2,2) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\path (0,2)--(1.2,2) node[midway,below] {$6\text{ m}$};
\path (-1.2,1) node[left] {$8\text{ m}$};
\path (0,0) node[below] {unpainted bottom};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A cylinder of radius $3$ cm and height $4$ cm stands centrally on the flat face of a hemisphere of radius $5$ cm. Find the total outside surface area, correct to $1$ decimal place.

Axial cross-section:
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.5,0)--(1.5,0);
\draw (-1.5,0) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=1.5];
\draw (-0.9,0)--(-0.9,1.5)--(0.9,1.5)--(0.9,0);
\path (0,1.5)--(0.9,1.5) node[midway,above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,0)--(1.5,0) node[midway,below] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (-0.9,0.75) node[left] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
